I get dressed and fetch my dark green coat.
I really do not feel well.
I walk very slowly to the doctor's practice.
Fortunately, it is not far from my flat.
I open the door and go to the reception.
"Good morning, I have an appointment for half past ten," I say.
"My name is Maya Flores."
The receptionist types something into her computer.
"Good morning, Frau Flores," she says.
"Do you have your insurance card with you?"
"Yes, here it is," I answer.
I give her my insurance card.
She puts the card into a small device on the desk.
It beeps quietly, and she gives the card back to me.
"You should take a seat in the waiting room," she says.
"The doctor will call you shortly."
"Thank you," I answer quietly, because my throat hurts so much.
